{# Shared page-transition overlay. Included (at build time, not fetched at
   runtime) into every page's <body> so it's part of the very first paint —
   no flash of the bare page before it appears. Its default CSS state is
   fully covering the screen; a CSS animation reveals the page moments
   after load, and js/script.js re-covers the screen the same way before
   navigating to another page, so the whole site always transitions with
   a single consistent "moving down" motion. See css/style.css for the
   .page-transition rules and js/script.js for the navigation handling.

   The logo is a separate element, not nested inside the sliding panel —
   its own fixed positioning keeps it correctly centered on screen, and
   its animation moves it in exact sync with the panel's slide (same
   top-to-bottom translate, timing and easing), so the two travel as one
   piece with no fading involved. #}
<div class="page-transition" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<img src="assets/logo.png" alt="" class="page-transition__logo" aria-hidden="true">